r del calcio (CASR).", "PARATIROIDECTOMÍA:La paratiroidectomía es una intervención quirúrgica que puede beneficiar a pacientes con hiperparatiroidismo primario leve y hipercalcemia hipocalciúrica familiar.", "CASR:El gen receptor sensor del calcio (CASR) es responsable de la regulación del calcio en el cuerpo y su mutación puede causar hipercalcemia hipocalciúrica familiar.", "PTHRP:PTHRP, or parathyroid hormone-related peptide, is a protein that plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body. It is particularly noted for its association with malignancies, as it can lead to hypercalcemia, a condition characterized by elevated calcium levels in the blood. This effect is especially observed in patients with solid tumors that are not metastatic. PTHrP's ability to induce hypercalcemia highlights its importance in the context of certain cancers and underscores its relevance in medical discussions surrounding tumor-related calcium dysregulation.", "HYPERCALCEMIA RELACIONADA CON PTHRP:La hipercalcemia relacionada con PTHrP elevada es una condición que representa hasta el 80% de los pacientes con hipercalcemia de malignidad.", "HYPERCALCEMIA DE MALIGNIDAD:La hipercalcemia de malignidad es una condición médica que se presenta en pacientes con cáncer, donde la hipercalcemia es causada por mecanismos relacionados con tumores.", "SPECT:SPECT, which stands for Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography, is a nuclear imaging technique that generates three-dimensional images of the body. This advanced imaging modality is often utilized in conjunction with other imaging techniques to enhance diagnostic accuracy. SPECT is particularly valuable in improving the detection of parathyroid glands, among other applications, making it a crucial tool in medical imaging.", "GAMMAGRAFÍA CON SESTAMIBI:Gammagrafía con sestamibi is a type of imaging test used to locate parathyroid adenomas in patients suspected of having hyperparathyroidism.", "CÁNCER ESOFÁGICO:Cáncer esofágico es una enfermedad maligna que afecta el esófago, un órgano crucial en el sistema digestivo. Esta condición puede tener efectos significativos sobre el estado nutricional de los pacientes, ya que puede llevar a complicaciones que afectan la ingesta y absorción de nutrientes. Además, se ha observado que el cáncer esofágico puede estar asociado con la hipercalcemia, una condición caracterizada por niveles elevados de calcio en la sangre. Los estudios también indican que el consumo de carne roja y procesada está relacionado con un aumento en el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, un tipo específico de cáncer esofágico. En resumen, el cáncer esofágico no solo representa un desafío médico en términos de tratamiento y manejo, sino que también plantea preocupaciones nutricionales significativas para quienes lo padecen.", "CÁNCER DE CUELLO UTERINO BULBAR:Cáncer de cuello uterino bulbar is a type of cancer that can cause hypercalcemia.", "CÁNCER RENAL:Cáncer renal is a type of kidney cancer that is often associated with hypercalcemia. It has been linked to obesity, which significantly increases the mortality risk for those affected. Research has also explored the relationship between cáncer renal and dietary factors, particularly the consumption of fish and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, studies indicate that a diet rich in plant fiber and legumes may reduce the risk of developing this type of cancer.", "CÁNCER VESICAL:Cáncer vesical, or bladder cancer, is a type of malignancy that can be influenced by various dietary factors. Research suggests that the antioxidant properties found in fruits and vegetables may play a role in reducing the risk of developing bladder cancer, particularly among smokers. Additionally, this type of cancer is associated with certain health complications, such as hypercalcemia. Furthermore, there is an increased risk of bladder cancer linked to the consumption of processed meats. Overall, dietary choices, particularly the intake of antioxidants from fruits and vegetables, are significant factors in the risk profile for cáncer vesical."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}